evidence.quote:
This follows the Bradley-Terry model (Bradley and Terry, 1952) for estimating score functions
from pairwise preferences, and is the specialization of the Luce-Shephard choice rule (Luce, 2005;
Shepard, 1957) to preferences over trajectory segments.

TAMER (Knox, 2012;
Knox and Stone, 2013) also learn a reward function, however they consider much simpler settings
where the desired policy can be learned relatively quickly.

